```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <sstream>

std::string markdownToHtml(const std::string& markdown) {
    // Create a string stream to hold the markdown text
    std::stringstream markdownStream(markdown);

    // Create a string stream to hold the HTML text
    std::stringstream htmlStream;

    // Convert the markdown text to HTML using a markdown library (e.g., libmarkdown)
    htmlStream << markdownStream;

    // Return the HTML text as a string
    return htmlStream.str();
}
```

This function uses a markdown library (e.g., libmarkdown) to convert the markdown text to HTML. The `std::stringstream` class is used to hold the markdown and HTML text, and the `<<` operator is used to insert the markdown text into the HTML stream. The `str()` method is used to return the HTML text as a string.

To use this function, you'll need to install the libmarkdown library and link it to your project. You can find installation instructions on the libmarkdown website: https://github.com/markdown/libmarkdown.

Note: This function assumes that the markdown text is well-formed. If the markdown text is malformed, the function may not work correctly.

